    {
      "id": "case-build-compose-service-shape",
      "behaviors": [
        "bhv-build-image-parity"
      ],
      "context": [],
      "scenarioContext": {
        "sdim-operation": "build",
        "sdim-config-source": "compose",
        "sdim-container-state": "none",
        "sdim-features": "none",
        "sdim-layering": "single",
        "sdim-output-mode": "structured"
      },
      "inputClass": "valid",
      "oracleType": "spec-expectation",
      "resourceGroup": "docker-shared",
      "operations": [
        {
          "id": "op-build",
          "subcommand": "build",
          "argv": [
            "--workspace-folder",
            "${WORKSPACE}",
            "--output-format",
            "json"
          ],
          "fixtures": [
            "fx-build-compose"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "expected": [
        {
          "channel": "chan-exit-code",
          "operation": "op-build",
          "assertion": {
            "equals": 0
          }
        },
        {
          "channel": "chan-structured-output",
          "operation": "op-build",
          "assertion": {
            "jsonSubset": {
              "outcome": "success"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "channel": "chan-stdout",
          "operation": "op-build",
          "assertion": {
            "matches": "\"imageName\"\\s*:\\s*\\[\\s*\"[^\"]*-app\""
          }
        }
      ],
      "cleanup": {
        "containers": true,
        "images": false,
        "networks": true,
        "volumes": true,
        "tempdir": true
      },
      "notes": "Covers the high-risk triple `hrt-build-compose-no-features-structured`. Building a Compose configuration has to resolve the SERVICE's build shape rather than the top-level one; the `-app` suffix on the reported image name is what shows which of the two was read, and `outcome` alone would not — a build of the wrong thing succeeds too. The image name's leading segment carries a workspace-derived hash and is deliberately left unpinned. Spec-expectation rather than differential because the structured rendering is reached by a flag the two CLIs spell differently, and the runner sends one argv to both sides."
    },
