        }
      ],
      "cleanup": {
        "containers": true,
        "images": false,
        "networks": true,
        "volumes": true,
        "tempdir": true
      },
      "notes": "Error-path tier, build stage, with the build ARGUMENT as the thing under test. The Dockerfile's `RUN` exits non-zero only when `CONF_FAIL=1` reaches it, and the configuration is the only place that value comes from — so a CLI that dropped `build.args` would SUCCEED here. The failure is therefore evidence that the argument was delivered, which the ordinary build-args case (`case-tier1-build-args-subst`, a configuration comparison) cannot supply: it observes the resolved document, not what the builder received. Both sides fail (verified against oracle 0.87.0)."
    },
