        "images": false,
        "networks": true,
        "volumes": true,
        "tempdir": true
      },
      "notes": "Error-path tier, build stage: `build.target` names a stage the Dockerfile does not define. Nothing about the document is wrong and BOTH CLIs read it without complaint — the target is a free-form string, and no reader can know which stages exist until the builder resolves the Dockerfile graph. That is the point: the failure is unreachable until after the stage where the reference is most lenient, which is exactly where parity used to stop comparing. Both sides fail (verified against oracle 0.87.0 in an isolated workspace)."
    }
